  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Ruby. You're verified, and I'm sorry the order was so late.\n\nI checked the delivery records for your Pho Real order (K-8401). It was promised for 6:30 PM, and the courier handed it over at 7:14 PM. That makes it 44 minutes late. Our records show it as slightly under an hour, not over.\n\nUnder our policy, a delivery 16 to 44 minutes late gets account credit equal to the delivery fee. I've added **$3.99** to your account as credit. You can use it on a future order.\n\nI can't offer more than that for this delivery. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Hmm, it felt like well over an hour to me, so I'm surprised it's only 44 minutes. Still, I'll take your word on the records. I'd rather have the money on my card than store credit, though. Can you refund it to my card instead?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand, Ruby. It was probably a long wait, since you ordered at 5:40 PM. But I can't refund late-delivery compensation to your card. Our policy limits it to account credit. The $3.99 is already on your account and will apply to your next order.\n\nIf you're unhappy with this and want to talk to a person, I can pass your case to a human specialist. Or I can help with something else."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I get that it's policy. I'd still rather have it on my card, but store credit is fine. I don't really need to escalate this, so I'll just take the $3.99 and use it on my next order."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Okay, Ruby. The $3.99 credit is on your account and will be there for your next order. Thank you for your patience, and I'm sorry again about the delay. Enjoy the rest of your evening."
  }
